  "query_preview": "..Strong easterly gradients across the southwestern \nUnited States will continue through late Friday. Wind speeds by late \nthis morning had exceeded all guidance in a few places, enough to \nassume that this will continue for awhile. So, we issued a Wind \nAdvisory for our western zones for now. There is also indication \nthat a band of stronger winds will develop over southern Navajo and \nApache counties later tonight and more zones may need to be added.\n\nBy the start of the weekend, the easterlies will subside as a weak \nupper low off the Baja Peninsula gets picked up by an amplifying \neastern Pacific trough. This will, once again, pick up some tropical \nmoisture and slowly introduce shower chances back to our area. By \nearly next week, a strong trough will move into the remnant moisture \nand provide several days of showers and thunderstorms, possibly even \nthrough the end of the week. If this sounds familiar, it is, because \nwe just did it last week. Will this be a repeat? Maybe, stay tuned \nand find out!",
